-1-67"><label>8.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kahn</surname><given-names>C</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>Artificial intelligence in radiology: decision support systems</article-title><source>RadioGraphics</source><year>1994</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>849</fpage><lpage>61</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7938772</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b9-poljradiol-75-1-67"><label>9.</label><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rangayyan</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Press</surname><given-names>CRC</given-names></name></person-group><source>Biomedical image analysis</source><comment>Edited by</comment><publisher-loc>Boca Raton, Fla.</publisher-loc><publisher-name>CRC Press</publisher-name><year>2005</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>1272</fpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="b10-poljradiol-75-1-67"><label>10.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gilbert</surname><given-names>FJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Lemke</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Computer-aided diagnosis</article-title><source>Br J Radiol</source><year>2005</year><volume>78</volume><fpage>S1</fpage><lpage>2</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="b11-poljradiol-75-1-67"><label>11.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sluimer</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Prokop</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Van Ginneken</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Toward automated segmentation of the pathological lung in CT</article-title><source>IEEE transactions on medical imaging</source><year>2005</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>1